Z||000007||Cooter||12-07-2000||11:22 PM||||I had a friend's Honda 600 F2 up to 130. It is really spooky to think that when going that fast, one little error and they pick you up with a spoon. I swore to never do that again! Had my Civic to 110, 88 GT/3.4 to 115 and the 'Burb to what ever it is when the speedo is pointed straight down (while pulling a double axle car trailer!), probably around 110.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroMaster88||12-07-2000||11:25 PM||||Well, I have had my 88 coupe up to only about 90 or 95, but I was not trying anything...<P>The fastest I have ever gone is 150 mph in my friends winter car.  HE has a 85 Fiero GT for a summer car, but his winter car is fast too!  It is a 97 Mitsubishi Eclipse GSX, can u say Turbocharged and all wheele drive????  We were racing a Mustang GT (about a 98) down a highway in downtown Clevland OH, and we beat him <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> .....The sunroof did not make it though....Driver tried to close it at 150, I told him it would not work! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||86SE||12-07-2000||11:27 PM||||56 once in a 55.  No cops, and had the petal to the plastic in 1st gear.... Never again will i go that fast..........In that gear anyways... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>Do my tail lights work?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||14
Z||000010||AkursedX||12-07-2000||11:55 PM||||In my 88GT I hit the 120mph mark.  But the fastest I've ever gone is 141mph in my dad's slighty massaged 1994 Chevy Caprice police version.  I didn't even have the pedal to the floor.  God I miss that car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000011||Shiner||12-08-2000||12:04 AM||||105 in the GT.  It was just purring along in fifth gear at that point.  Even took a few curves at that speed. Solid as a rock.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> I had my coupe up to god knows what.  It was at 4500rpm in 3rd gear (auto), which was nearing the 0 mark again.  <P> Once I get the GT back on the road with new paint, I will see if I can push the speedo past 120.  It had plenty of go left at 100  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||12-08-2000||12:13 AM||||Gone a bit past 100 a few times in the GT, and had the speedo needle pointing a little past straight down in the coupe once... then I realized that I have enough trouble with cops as it is, so I try not to do that too much anymore  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
