Z||000019||82-T/A||12-08-2000||08:22 AM||||UR2BITME, I totally know what you mean..<P>The fastest I've ever taken my 87 Fiero was 125 something or rather miles an hour. I've had it pegged at 120, and it would keep going, so I'll say around 130 miles an hour.<P>But at that speed.... the engine tone tends to change.. it's loud.. but calmer than it is when your racing it.. kinda weird. Your car just seems to glide through the air. With my car, it felt more stable at triple digit speeds than it did when going slower... but I soo totally know what you mean.<P><BR>My 1985 Fiero GT 4-Speed with the 4.10s that i used to own.. I would take that to 100 all the time. It gripped teh road well and man.. that thing could really get up there quick.<BR>I would hit the rev limiter in 4th gear. <BR>I think the fastest it would go was probably around at the very most.. 110 miles an hour. Hard to tell though since the gage only went to 85. But it had no problems getting up there.<P>You know how in like an auto Fiero, it gets to 100 no problem, and then takes quite a bit longer getting to 120?<P>Well the 85 with the 4.10s would get from 90-110 just as quickly as it did from like... 30-60.<P>Pretty cool.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000020||Phil||12-08-2000||08:48 AM||||120 mph speed limiter. Don't ask how I know.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/New-sig.jpg"> <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
