Z||000022||bHooper||12-08-2000||09:29 AM||||when my GT was younger, and the 2.8 had a little more umph, there was a section of country road that i always hit 113 mph on.<P>however, my dad had it running at 118 on I-95 on the way back from Floriday, one time... coulda gone faster, too.<P>a fella i work with, once got a ride in a Lamborgini (i know thats not the right spelling, but i have only had one cup of coffee), while in italy, and got up to 193 mph!  he said it scared the p!$$ out of him!<P>i can imagine!<P>hoop<P>||||reg||1
Z||000023||Tigger||12-08-2000||09:35 AM||||I really don't know for sure, still have the 85 speedo.  All I know, the headlights pop, and the speedo needle goes around almost back to 0.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Probably around 115.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000024||stsmithgt||12-08-2000||09:38 AM||||Well, in my GT I didn't go over 115 mph.  The engine has too many miles on it to push for more.  Although back in those days when you think you're invincible,  My brother took out his 1970 R/T Challenger with a 440 six pack, and we speed that thing up to about 160+ mph.  The scariest part was that I was in the back seat.  The engine put out about 600 hp. and had a gear ratio for the freeway. 275's?  The power was put through a M22 rock crusher 4 speed w/pistol grip.  He had the tallest tires he could fit in the fenders on their so I'm not sure how fast we were really going.  That's just what the speedo was saying.  The scary part was they were 50 series Kelly Super Chargers <B>BIOS PLY! </B>, which I don't think were made to go that fast. We'd have to pick the back of the car off the ground while someone filled the air shocks up to keep them from rubbing on the fenders.  Ahhhhhh.. those were the days when 4 miles per gallon in town and 8 on the freeway were afforable.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">(1981)  I'll look for a picture of what's left of it when you get your throttle linkage caught open, slide down a bank, flip over, and hit a couple of trees.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Luckily my brother only got a black eye.(no seat belts on.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> ) <P><BR>mental note: give gaurdian angle a good Christmas present this year, drive safe.<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000025||Old Lar||12-08-2000||09:52 AM||||120+ in my 5 speed GT...ran out of room on the two lane highway. Don't know how fast I was at Gateway International Speedway at the FOCOA show in 98.<BR>140+ in an Opel GT at Riverside raceway back in the early 70's.<P>I don't go much over 100 now a days. Getting too old for that.||||reg||3
